 \mytriangle{red} Here you can learn how to add the elements of a list:
 \begin{solutionbox} \begin{center}\bf{List addition with Casio fx-9750GII}\end{center}\begin{enumerate}[label=\protect\circled{\color{white}\arabic*}]
 \item \begin{bf}Step one:\end{bf}   Press \keystroke{menu} and the key \keystroke{2} to access the list menu (stat). Type the List 1 values. \item \begin{bf}Step two:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{menu} and the key \keystroke{1} to access the run menu.
\item \begin{bf}Step two:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{OPTION} and \keystroke{F1} for the List menu. In this menu, you will see the \keystroke{   $\triangleright$ } key that leads to \keystroke{   Sum }, the sum function. Press it.
\item \begin{bf}Step three:\end{bf} Now press \keystroke{OPTION} and select List1. 
 \item \begin{bf}Step four:\end{bf} Press \keystroke{EXE} and you will obtain the result of adding all elements of List1.
 \end{enumerate}
\end{solutionbox}
